@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Experimental CS2 lane graph capture
+
+This local modification adds `extensions.cs2.lane_graph` to a `cmm-v1` export.
+The original `nodes`, `networks`, and `traffic` fields remain unchanged. It
+captures every real car `EdgeLane` on exported road edges, including partial
+lanes at ramps, and car `NodeLane` connectors with road path method owned by
+exported network nodes.
+
+`edge_lanes` records the lane entity ID/version, owning edge ID/version,
+start/end composition lane indexes, full path indexes, edge range, width,
+speed, car flags, and four Bezier control points. `connectors` records the
+node, source/target edge and lane indexes, full curve, path-method flags, and
+forbidden/unsafe/public-only status. The matching IDs are native game entity
+IDs, not the old traffic snapshot's `lane_index` buffer position.
+
+`stats.unresolved_connectors` counts car node lanes whose path endpoints do
+not resolve to two exported road edges. Some may legitimately lead to
+non-road or non-exported edges; inspect the count and sample connections
+before using this as a complete routing graph. `invalid_curves` counts
+non-finite source curves omitted from either array.
+
+The capture reads ECS data on the main game thread after all tracked jobs
+complete. No gameplay systems or traffic simulation are modified.
+
+## Local compile experiment
+
+The official project uses the CS2 Modding Toolchain. For this source-only
+export change, `StandaloneBuild.csproj` also compiles directly against the
+installed game's managed assemblies with a .NET 8 SDK. It targets net48 and
+emits `CS2/bin/Release/net48/CSLModernMapCs2.dll`.
+
+```
+dotnet build CS2/StandaloneBuild.csproj -c Release
+```
+
+If the game is installed elsewhere, pass `-p:ManagedDir="C:\path\to\Cities2_Data\Managed"`.
+This local compile passed with zero warnings and errors against the installed
+game assemblies on 2026-11-12. Runtime loading, export duration, output size,
+and lane-graph completeness have **not** yet been verified. Do not publish or
+replace the installed mod with this DLL before backing up the existing
+version and testing the export in the game.
